      "A second important principle: relaxation begins with certainty. Before asking a client to settle into a quiet hands-on service, remove as much preventable uncertainty as reasonably possible. The practitioner should answer predictable logistical questions before the client has to carry them mentally. This does not mean giving a long speech or narrating every future technique.",
